  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Psalms",
    "delineation": "Psalm",
    "number": 16,
    "summary": "A messianic psalm of David—He rejoices in the Saints who are on the earth, in his own future redemption from hell, in the fact that God will not suffer His Holy One (the Messiah) to see corruption, and in the fulness of joy that is found in the Lord’s presence.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Preserve me, O God: for in thee do I put my trust.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 44,
            "end": 49,
            "text": "TG Trust in God."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "O my soul, thou hast said unto the Lord, Thou art my Lord: my goodness extendeth not to thee;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 59,
            "end": 61,
            "text": "HEB I have no good apart from Thee."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 10
          },
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 49
          },
          {
            "start": 71,
            "end": 80
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But to the saints that are in the earth, and to the excellent, in whom is all my delight.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 3
          },
          {
            "start": 23,
            "end": 26
          },
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 47
          },
          {
            "start": 71,
            "end": 73
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Their sorrows shall be multiplied that hasten after another god: their drink offerings of blood will I not offer, nor take up their names into my lips.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 60,
            "end": 63,
            "text": "Ex. 34:14 (13–17); 2 Ne. 9:37 (37–38); Alma 7:6; D&C 124:84; Abr. 1:11 (11–12, 15)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 38
          },
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 51
          },
          {
            "start": 60,
            "end": 63
          },
          {
            "start": 63,
            "end": 64
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The Lord is the portion of mine inheritance and of my cup: thou maintainest my lot.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 23,
            "text": "Ps. 73:26; 119:57."
          },
          {
            "start": 32,
            "end": 43,
            "text": "Deut. 18:2."
          },
          {
            "start": 64,
            "end": 82,
            "text": "HEB holdest my fate."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 11
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The lines are fallen unto me in pleasant places; yea, I have a goodly heritage.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 48
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "I will bless the Lord, who hath given me counsel: my reins also instruct me in the night seasons.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "I have set the Lord always before me: because he is at my right hand, I shall not be moved.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 19,
            "text": "Acts 2:25 (25–31)."
          },
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 68,
            "text": "Ps. 109:31."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 51
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore my heart is glad, and my glory rejoiceth: my flesh also shall rest in hope.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 55,
            "end": 60,
            "text": "TG Resurrection."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For thou wilt not leave my soul in hell; neither wilt thou suffer thine Holy One to see corruption.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 18,
            "end": 23,
            "text": "2 Ne. 4:31 (31–32)."
          },
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 31,
            "text": "Ps. 30:3."
          },
          {
            "start": 35,
            "end": 39,
            "text": "TG Damnation; Hell; Spirits in Prison."
          },
          {
            "start": 72,
            "end": 80,
            "text": "TG Jesus Christ, Resurrection."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Thou wilt shew me the path of life: in thy presence is fulness of joy; at thy right hand there are pleasures for evermore.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 43,
            "end": 51,
            "text": "TG God, Presence of."
          },
          {
            "start": 55,
            "end": 62,
            "text": "TG Exaltation."
          },
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 69,
            "text": "TG Joy."
          },
          {
            "start": 99,
            "end": 108,
            "text": "Ps. 36:8."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
